As calls mount for accountability over the <span class="caps">ICE</span> killing of Lorenzo Salgado Araujo in Houston, we speak with Democratic Congressmember Al Green, who represents Texas&#8217;s 9th Congressional District. He demands an independent investigation into the shooting to stop &#8220;an attempt to cover up&#8221; the killing by the Trump administration.</p>
<p>Democratic lawmakers led by the Congressional Hispanic Caucus will hold a public hearing in Houston on Friday to gather testimony from community members about Salgado Araujo&#8217;s killing. Green, one of the longest-serving Black members in Congress, highlights the importance of solidarity between different communities facing oppression.</p>
<p>&#8220;Invidious discrimination is the common enemy for Latinos and African Americans, and we have to confront this common enemy together,&#8221; says Green. &#8220;We cannot allow people to segregate us.&#8221;
